@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] handbook-evidence
Handbook statements MUST distinguish current implementation, accepted design and
executed acceptance. State diagrams MUST preserve the distinction between intent,
physical observation, workflow progress and cleanup authority.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] handbook-static-private-content
Chapters MUST contain reviewed repository documentation and synthetic configuration
examples only. Credentials and private runtime evidence MUST NOT be included.
Handbook content MUST NOT be served through public documentation or static routes.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:performance] handbook-section-delivery
The contents page MUST NOT send chapter bodies. A section page MUST contain only
its selected chapter, and navigation MUST remove the previous section's diagrams.
Source chapter links MUST resolve to authenticated section URLs.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:verification] handbook-required-architecture-views
Ash domains and deployment topology MUST have source-derived visual inventories,
maintained interaction diagrams, concise responsibility and authority explanations,
and explicit verification gaps. Domains MUST NOT imply separate deployments;
declared topology MUST NOT imply live health or physical failure acceptance.
